{
  "beats": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "startTick": 96,
      "endTick": 1480,
      "narration": "Picture electricity as water flowing through a pipe. The push is voltage, the flow is current."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "startTick": 1576,
      "endTick": 3040,
      "narration": "A resistor is a narrow section of pipe. It fights the flow, so less current gets through."
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "startTick": 3136,
      "endTick": 4000,
      "narration": "Ohm's law ties them together: voltage equals current times resistance."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "startTick": 4096,
      "endTick": 5656,
      "narration": "So if you double the resistance and keep the voltage the same, the current is cut in half."
    }
  ],
